; Copyright (c) 2026 Martino Pilia
;
; EMPHASIS state machine: drives the TXE amplitude-select pin from the CPU
; annotation stream (one bit per data bit: the leading-half emphasis, packed
; LSB-first). TXE high = full amplitude, low = reduced tail. The trailing half of
; every bit is hard-coded full.
;
; 120 MHz clock, 12 cycles/bit, phase-matched to the LEVEL SM. The LEVEL SM spends
; its first 2 cycles per bit on out/jmp (pins holding the previous trailing half),
; then drives the leading half for cycles [2,8) and the trailing half for [8,12).
; This SM mirrors that phase so the reduced leading-half window lines up:
;   set[1] : full for cycles [0,2)  (trailing-half spillover; always full)
;   out[5] : leading-half emphasis for cycles [2,8)
;   set[3] : full for cycles [8,12) (trailing half)
; Both SMs are started with their TX FIFOs pre-filled and enabled in sync so the
; phase holds from the first bit; the alignment is confirmed on-target by the
; DBG_PADOUT self-test.

.program tx_emphasis

.wrap_target
    set pins, 1 [1]          ; full  (cycles [0,2))
    out pins, 1 [5]          ; leading-half emphasis (autopull, LSB-first)  [2,8)
    set pins, 1 [3]          ; full  (cycles [8,12))
.wrap
